<section data-label="No process" data-speaker-notes="Key reframe: the problem isn't the model, it's the lack of process. Almost nobody learned to orchestrate AI like a pipeline — we ask for everything at once, in a single thread, with no steps and no review. A team takes the process for granted; with AI you have to build it by hand. Three symptoms: all at once, no plan to go back to, and it reviews itself." style="color:#dfe4ec;font-family:'Instrument Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;box-sizing:border-box;padding:92px 110px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;position:relative;overflow:hidden;background-color:#0b0c11;background-image:radial-gradient(1100px 640px at 86% -14%,oklch(70% .15 28/.17),transparent 66%),radial-gradient(820px 560px at 2% 112%,oklch(66% .13 28/.10),transparent 70%),radial-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,.05) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:auto,auto,34px 34px;">
  <div style="position:absolute;top:50px;right:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:18px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#828b99;font-weight:700;"><span style="display:flex;gap:3px;"><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(76% .145 75)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(74% .145 300)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(74% .145 245)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(76% .145 155)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(72% .145 25)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(75% .145 340)"></span></span>ASDT</div>
  <div class="au" style="max-width:1380px;margin-bottom:48px;">
    <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(76% .14 28);margin:0 0 24px;font-weight:500;">03 / 13 · the real problem</p>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:66px;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f3f6fb;margin:0;text-wrap:balance;">The problem isn't the AI. It's that nobody builds it a process.</h2>
    <p style="font-size:29px;line-height:1.45;color:#aab2c0;margin:28px 0 0;max-width:1300px;">The AI is brilliant. But almost nobody learned to orchestrate it like a pipeline — and without a process, even brilliance derails.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="display:flex;gap:24px;">
    <div class="as d1" style="flex:1;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:16px;padding:30px 32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;margin-bottom:14px;"><span style="font-size:24px;">🌀</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:29px;font-weight:600;color:oklch(80% .12 28);">All at once, in one thread</span></div>
      <p style="font-size:23px;line-height:1.45;color:#b5bdca;margin:0 0 18px;">We throw the whole task at it and expect magic: no steps, no order, no review.</p>
      <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;color:#8b94a2;margin:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);padding-top:18px;"><strong style="color:oklch(80% .1 28);font-weight:600;">Example:</strong> «build the login» → it attempted design, backend and security in a single pass.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="as d2" style="flex:1;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:16px;padding:30px 32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;margin-bottom:14px;"><span style="font-size:24px;">🗺️</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:29px;font-weight:600;color:oklch(80% .12 28);">No plan to go back to</span></div>
      <p style="font-size:23px;line-height:1.45;color:#b5bdca;margin:0 0 18px;">It shipped because it worked — not because someone decided it should be that way.</p>
      <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;color:#8b94a2;margin:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);padding-top:18px;"><strong style="color:oklch(80% .1 28);font-weight:600;">Example:</strong> it built a whole password-reset flow when you only asked for a «forgot my password» link.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="as d3" style="flex:1;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:16px;padding:30px 32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;margin-bottom:14px;"><span style="font-size:24px;">🪞</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:29px;font-weight:600;color:oklch(80% .12 28);">It reviews itself</span></div>
      <p style="font-size:23px;line-height:1.45;color:#b5bdca;margin:0 0 18px;">A single viewpoint can't see its own mistakes. It's not the model's fault: it's a hole in the process.</p>
      <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;color:#8b94a2;margin:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);padding-top:18px;"><strong style="color:oklch(80% .1 28);font-weight:600;">Example:</strong> whoever wrote the code also reviewed it — and didn't notice it stored the passwords in plain sight.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:25px;line-height:1.4;color:#cdd4df;margin:30px 0 0;text-align:center;font-weight:500;">The good news: a process can be learned. <strong style="color:#f3f6fb;font-weight:700;">That's exactly what ASDT builds.</strong></p>
<aside class="notes">Key reframe: the problem isn't the model, it's the lack of process. Almost nobody learned to orchestrate AI like a pipeline — we ask for everything at once, in a single thread, with no steps and no review. A team takes the process for granted; with AI you have to build it by hand. Three symptoms: all at once, no plan to go back to, and it reviews itself.</aside>
</section>

