<section data-label="Context" data-speaker-notes="The root problem with agents is the context limit: the AI's working memory is finite. If you cram everything into a single thread, it fills up, forgets and gets worse — slower and more expensive. ASDT solves it with subagents: each step is a small task with clean context and its result is passed through a written document. This is what makes the seven specialists work. For a PM: it's like a whiteboard that fills up; better to have several clean, focused whiteboards." style="color:#dfe4ec;font-family:'Instrument Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;box-sizing:border-box;padding:72px 96px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;position:relative;overflow:hidden;background-color:#0b0c11;background-image:radial-gradient(1100px 640px at 88% -14%,oklch(74% .15 245/.16),transparent 66%),radial-gradient(820px 560px at 0% 112%,oklch(68% .13 245/.10),transparent 70%),radial-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,.05) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:auto,auto,34px 34px;">
  <div style="position:absolute;top:50px;right:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:18px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#828b99;font-weight:700;"><span style="display:flex;gap:3px;"><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(76% .145 75)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(74% .145 300)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(74% .145 245)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(76% .145 155)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(72% .145 25)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(75% .145 340)"></span></span>ASDT</div>
  <div class="au" style="margin-bottom:28px;">
    <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(78% .12 245);margin:0 0 18px;font-weight:500;">09 / 13 · the technical bit, made simple</p>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:60px;line-height:1.03;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f3f6fb;margin:0;text-wrap:balance;max-width:1300px;">The real bottleneck: context</h2>
    <p style="font-size:26px;line-height:1.4;color:#9aa3b2;margin:16px 0 0;max-width:1180px;">Every AI has a limited working memory. When it fills up, it starts to forget — and that's where quality falls off.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:stretch;margin-bottom:22px;">
    <div class="al d1" style="flex:1;background:oklch(70% .12 28/.06);border:1px solid oklch(72% .14 28/.4);border-radius:16px;padding:26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;margin-bottom:14px;"><span style="font-size:24px;">⚠️</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:27px;font-weight:600;color:#f3f6fb;">Everything in one thread</span></div>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;opacity:.32;margin-bottom:6px;">
        <div style="height:12px;width:88%;border-radius:4px;background:oklch(72% .14 28/.7);"></div>
        <div style="height:12px;width:74%;border-radius:4px;background:oklch(72% .14 28/.7);"></div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono';font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.03em;color:oklch(80% .12 28);margin:0 0 8px;">⤴ this has already left the window</p>
      <div style="border:1.5px dashed oklch(74% .14 28/.6);border-radius:10px;padding:11px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;">
        <div style="height:12px;width:100%;border-radius:4px;background:oklch(72% .13 28/.5);"></div>
        <div style="height:12px;width:92%;border-radius:4px;background:oklch(72% .13 28/.5);"></div>
        <div style="height:12px;width:97%;border-radius:4px;background:oklch(72% .13 28/.5);"></div>
        <div style="height:12px;width:85%;border-radius:4px;background:oklch(72% .13 28/.5);"></div>
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;"><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono';font-size:13px;color:oklch(80% .12 28);">context window · FULL</span></div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:21px;line-height:1.45;color:#b5bdca;margin:16px 0 0;">Message 200: it's forgotten message 5. It contradicts itself, slows down and <strong style="color:#e7ebf2;font-weight:600;">costs more</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ar d2" style="flex:1;background:oklch(70% .12 155/.06);border:1px solid oklch(74% .145 155/.4);border-radius:16px;padding:26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;margin-bottom:14px;"><span style="font-size:24px;">✅</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:27px;font-weight:600;color:#f3f6fb;">Split into subagents</span></div>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px;">
        <span style="background:rgba(255,255,255,.05);border:1px solid oklch(74% .145 155/.5);border-radius:9px;padding:8px 13px;font-size:17px;color:#dfe4ec;">🧩 task A · clean</span>
        <span style="background:rgba(255,255,255,.05);border:1px solid oklch(74% .145 155/.5);border-radius:9px;padding:8px 13px;font-size:17px;color:#dfe4ec;">🧩 task B · clean</span>
        <span style="background:rgba(255,255,255,.05);border:1px solid oklch(74% .145 155/.5);border-radius:9px;padding:8px 13px;font-size:17px;color:#dfe4ec;">🧩 task C · clean</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:oklch(70% .12 155/.1);border:1px solid oklch(74% .145 155/.45);border-radius:10px;padding:12px 14px;">
        <span style="font-size:22px;">📄</span><span style="font-size:18px;color:#cdd4df;">each one leaves its result written and passes it to the next</span>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:21px;line-height:1.45;color:#b5bdca;margin:16px 0 0;">Each subagent starts <strong style="color:oklch(82% .1 155);font-weight:600;">from scratch and focused</strong>. Memory never saturates because it never loads everything at once.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;gap:18px;">
    <div class="au d3" style="flex:1;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-top:3px solid oklch(74% .145 245);border-radius:14px;padding:20px 24px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px;"><span style="font-size:22px;">🧠</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#f3f6fb;">Working memory</span></div>
      <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.4;color:#aab2c0;margin:0 0 10px;">What the AI can hold «in mind» at once. It's finite.</p>
      <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono';font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.03em;color:oklch(80% .1 245);margin:0;">= context window · measured in tokens</p>
    </div>
    <div class="au d4" style="flex:1;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-top:3px solid oklch(72% .145 28);border-radius:14px;padding:20px 24px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px;"><span style="font-size:22px;">📉</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#f3f6fb;">When it saturates</span></div>
      <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.4;color:#aab2c0;margin:0 0 10px;">Long thread = forgets, mixes things up and answers worse.</p>
      <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono';font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.03em;color:oklch(80% .11 28);margin:0;">= «lost in the middle» · context rot</p>
    </div>
    <div class="au d5" style="flex:1;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-top:3px solid oklch(76% .145 155);border-radius:14px;padding:20px 24px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px;"><span style="font-size:22px;">✂️</span><span style="font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#f3f6fb;">The way out: divide</span></div>
      <p style="font-size:20px;line-height:1.4;color:#aab2c0;margin:0 0 10px;">Small tasks, each with its own fresh context.</p>
      <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono';font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.03em;color:oklch(80% .1 155);margin:0;">= subagents + handoff via document</p>
    </div>
  </div>
<aside class="notes">The root problem with agents is the context limit: the AI's working memory is finite. If you cram everything into a single thread, it fills up, forgets and gets worse — slower and more expensive. ASDT solves it with subagents: each step is a small task with clean context and its result is passed through a written document. This is what makes the seven specialists work. For a PM: it's like a whiteboard that fills up; better to have several clean, focused whiteboards.</aside>
</section>

<section data-label="Memory" data-speaker-notes="In practice: AI forgets; long sessions lose judgment. Each step starts with clean context and hands off through a written document. Documents survive, conversations don't." style="color:#dfe4ec;font-family:'Instrument Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;box-sizing:border-box;padding:92px 110px;display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:80px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;background-color:#0b0c11;background-image:radial-gradient(1100px 640px at 88% -14%,oklch(74% .15 75/.15),transparent 66%),radial-gradient(820px 560px at 0% 112%,oklch(68% .13 75/.10),transparent 70%),radial-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,.05) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:auto,auto,34px 34px;">
  <div style="position:absolute;top:50px;right:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:18px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#828b99;font-weight:700;"><span style="display:flex;gap:3px;"><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(76% .145 75)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(74% .145 300)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(74% .145 245)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(76% .145 155)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(72% .145 25)"></span><span style="width:6px;height:15px;border-radius:2px;background:oklch(75% .145 340)"></span></span>ASDT</div>
  <div class="al" style="flex:1;">
    <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(78% .145 75);margin:0 0 24px;font-weight:500;">10 / 13 · the memory problem</p>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:60px;line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f3f6fb;margin:0;text-wrap:balance;max-width:840px;">AI forgets. Long sessions don't just lose data — they lose judgment.</h2>
    <p style="font-size:27px;line-height:1.5;color:#aab2c0;margin:30px 0 0;max-width:840px;"><strong style="color:oklch(80% .12 75);font-weight:600;">In practice:</strong> each step starts with a clean, bounded context, and hands off to the next through a written document. The work lives in documents — not in a chat that may not exist tomorrow.</p>
    <p style="font-size:24px;line-height:1.5;color:#8b94a2;margin:24px 0 0;max-width:840px;">Ask a long chat «use the auth pattern we agreed on» and by message 200 it's forgotten which one — and invents a new one. A written document never forgets.</p>
  </div>
